## What upstream did with ours

The release notes say they took PRs 147-152 and issue 146. Measured against
`u61-candidate` (U60 + PRs 147-152), file by file over the 20 files the
candidate touches:

    15 byte-identical   Fireworks, the eleven fat16 fixtures,
                        app-runner-frame.expected, raytracer-test.{codex,expected}
     4 prose only       GuiOpening, Raytracer, AppRunner, app-runner-frame.codex:
                        our prose paragraphs deleted, no code changed
     1 code changed     ZigEmitter.codex: PR 147 made OPT-IN

PR 147 as landed: the deck report goes to fd 3 only when `CODEX_DECK_REPORT=1`
is in the environment (byte-exact; `01` does not count). To read the
environment, the emitted `main` now takes `std.process.Init.Minimal` and stores
`environ` in a new prelude part, `cx_environ`. Read, not yet run beyond the
probes below:

- `main`'s text is scanned for shake roots (ZigEmitter `zig-mask-hi ns
  main-text`), so `cx_environ` is kept in every program.
- `Init.Minimal` and `Environ.block.slice` exist in zig 0.16.0; the scan sits
  under a comptime `os.tag == .linux`, so Windows never analyses it.
- 112 prelude parts against the 128 the two-mask shake carries.
- The comment on `zig-p-cx-deck-report` still says "only when it was open at
  the first cx_deck_set" and does not mention the variable. Prose, theirs.

Ours to follow: nothing of ours reads CX-DECK as telemetry. The two filters that
drop it (curated `arms/ir-interp`, a comment in codex-wasm-transpiler
`build.py`) go when the bundles are rebuilt at U61.

