## PR 147 as landed, run

The new `codexzig` is itself an emitted program with a deck. Transpiling
safari's `SafariSpec.codex` (1,058,484 bytes): unset, 0 CX-DECK lines on fd 3;
`CODEX_DECK_REPORT=1` with fd 3 open, 89 lines, last `used=9437392`. The zig it
emits is byte-identical either way. On a small unit (p3) no setting reports,
because the deck never passes the 1 MB stride -- a negative that needed the
positive control to mean anything.
